WEBVTT

00:00:27.872 --> 00:00:31.874
David has been a political and cultural
columnist for "The New York Times,"

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.825
and he’s the author
of several blockbuster books

00:00:34.849 --> 00:00:38.618
that have really helped shape-shift
a lot of people’s worldviews,

00:00:38.642 --> 00:00:42.223
books like "Bobos in Paradise,"
"The Social Animal,"

00:00:42.247 --> 00:00:44.467
and "The Road to Character."

00:00:45.064 --> 00:00:49.878
Traditionally, David’s politics have been
seen as a little right of center,

00:00:49.902 --> 00:00:54.242
but what’s most striking to me about him
is how broad his thinking is.

00:00:54.266 --> 00:00:56.549
More than almost any other writer I know,

00:00:56.573 --> 00:01:00.590
he has a talent for synthesizing
ideas from different fields --